---------- ThoughtEvent (rgroup_substitution) ----------
I need to identify the 4 product variants (43-46) from molecular_recognition and derive their R-groups against the product template.

Looking at the bboxes:
- bbox_0 (y=208, x=0): product 43 — `CC(C)(C)OC(=O)CNC(=O)CN=[N+]=[N-]` (R1=H, R2=H)
- bbox_2 (y=208, x=266): product 44 — `C[C@H](NC(=O)CN=[N+]=[N-])C(=O)OC(C)(C)C` (R1=H, R2=Me)
- bbox_4 (y=198, x=546): product 45 — `CCCCOC(=O)[C@H](CC(C)C)NC(=O)CN=[N+]=[N-]` (R1=H, R2=iBu) — note: tBu was misread as butyl
- bbox_5 (y=198, x=842): product 46 — `CCCCOC(=O)[C@H](CC(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](C)N=[N+]=[N-]` (R1=Me, R2=iBu)

The MolNexTR products for 45 and 46 show `CCCCOC(=O)` (n-butyl) instead of `OC(C)(C)C` (tert-butyl) — this is a recognition error since the scheme uses O-t-Bu. But per the golden rule, I use MolNexTR's SMILES verbatim.

Let me derive substituents. The MolNexTR products for 43 and 44 have explicit H at R1 (no substituent shown), so the template-matching may need stripping. Let me try.
